mented in 7K LOC and integrates with PyTorch, TensorFlow, and X-DeepLearning. Crux Daemon and Crux Transport modules handle job profiling, probing network paths, and enforcing decisions via RDMA APIs.\n\n6. Evaluation  \n- 6.1 Testbed: 96-GPU testbed shows up to 14.8% GPU utilization gain and 33% JCT reduction.  \n- 6.2 Trace Simulation: On a 2,000+ GPU cluster trace, Crux outperforms Sincronia, TACCL, and CASSINI by 4–23%.  \n- 6.3 Scheduler Compatibility: Crux boosts performance even when combined with HiveD or Muri.  \n- 6.4 GPU Intensity Visualization: Darker flow patterns correlate with higher GPU utilization under Crux.\n\n7. Discussions  \n- 7.1 Limitations: Crux simplifies complex overlap patterns; real-world variance may cause suboptimal prioritization.  \n- 7.2 Fairness: Higher priority jobs may slightly degrade others; fairness extensions possible.  \n- 7.3 Topology Adaptability: Crux’s design generalizes across Clos, double-sided, and potentially other topologies.\n\n8. Related Work  \nCrux differs from job-level schedulers and prior intra-job communication solutions. It also surpasses inter-job tools like CASSINI by using real-time GPU intensity metrics and adaptive scheduling.\n\n9. Conclusion  \nCrux introduces GPU intensity as a foundational metric for DLT communication scheduling. Through path selection, priority assignment, and priority compression, it significantly improves cluster GPU utilization.\n\nAppendices  \n- A: Proof that GPU intensity-based flow scheduling correlates with utilization.  \n- B: Theoretical grounding for DAG-based Max-K-Cut in priority compression."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Got it!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the primary goal of Crux in deep learning training clusters?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': ' goal goal of Crux is to to to to improve. the scheduling in deep. training) clusters and clusters.,,, the..'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which metric does Crux introduce to prioritize communicati